WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.975
Anybody can build an AI demo.

00:01.975 --> 00:08.791
Almost nobody can prove it survives a real customer. That's the whole game — and exactly why teams bring me in.

00:08.791 --> 00:16.114
I build the AI features and the agents. The retrieval that makes them accurate. The automations that run the work while you sleep.

00:16.114 --> 00:23.441
And the parts people forget one engineer can do — the website it all lives on, and the content engine that keeps it fed.

00:23.441 --> 00:32.115
Then the part that actually matters: I prove every piece works. Real evaluations, tests, and gates. Not "trust me" — a number you can see.

00:32.115 --> 00:39.349
Thirteen years in software quality. Two live products I run entirely on my own. This isn't theory — it ships.

00:39.349 --> 00:46.436
One engineer. The entire stack. Built, and proven. Bring me the AI feature you're not sure about.

